<title>ITALY: Italy names KPMG consultant for bourse sell-off.</title>
<headline>Italy names KPMG consultant for bourse sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury said on Thursday it had named KPMG Peat Marwick as financial consultant for the planned privatisation of its stock exchanges.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the group would assess the most appropriate method of carrying out the privatisation.  </p>
<p>&quot;KMPG-Peat Marwick will have the task of working out the most efficient method of the procedure for selling shares in companies managing the markets which will be set up by the stock market council,&quot; the Treasury statement said.</p>
<p>The stock market is expected to be privatised later this year.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 22501</p>
